        "key": "B",
        "text": "$9+3\\pi$"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$6+4\\pi$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$2+6\\pi$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$4\\sqrt3+4\\pi$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Hexagon plus six semicircles",
        "body": "The hexagon splits into 6 equilateral triangles of side 2, each of area $\\frac{\\sqrt3}4\\cdot4=\\sqrt3$, so the hexagon has area $6\\sqrt3$. Each semicircle has radius 1 and area $\\frac\\pi2$; six of them give $3\\pi$. Total $6\\sqrt3+3\\pi$.\n\n**Answer: (A) $6\\sqrt3+3\\pi$**"
      }
    ],
