    "prompt": "In $\\triangle ABC$, $AY=AZ$, $BX=BZ$ and $CX=CY$ (with $X$, $Y$, $Z$ on $BC$, $CA$, $AB$), and the sizes of two angles are as shown ($\\angle XZY=40^\\circ$ and $\\angle ZYX=75^\\circ$). The angle at $A$ is",
    "image": "qimages/samf/senior-1999-r1/q11.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "$50^\\circ$"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "$60^\\circ$"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$55^\\circ$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$52\\frac12^\\circ$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$57\\frac12^\\circ$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Isosceles base angles",
        "body": "Let $\\angle AZY=\\angle AYZ=a$, $\\angle BZX=\\angle BXZ=b$, $\\angle CXY=\\angle CYX=c$ (base angles of the three isosceles corner triangles). The straight angles at $Z$, $Y$, $X$ give $a+b=180^\\circ-40^\\circ=140^\\circ$, $a+c=180^\\circ-75^\\circ=105^\\circ$, and (as $\\angle ZXY=180^\\circ-40^\\circ-75^\\circ=65^\\circ$) $b+c=180^\\circ-65^\\circ=115^\\circ$. Adding: $a+b+c=180^\\circ$, so $a=65^\\circ$ ($=180^\\circ-115^\\circ$). The angle at $A$ is $180^\\circ-2a=50^\\circ$.\n\n**Answer: (A) $50^\\circ$**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "geometry"
    ],
