      {
        "title": "Count the rings",
        "body": "A shape with $n$ coins per side is a centre coin surrounded by rings. Ring $k$ (the ring $k$ steps from the centre) has $6k$ coins. A shape with 21 coins along each side has rings $k=1,\\dots,20$, so the total is $1+6(1+2+\\cdots+20)=1+6\\cdot210=1261$. (Check: $n=2$: $1+6=7$; $n=3$: $1+6+12=19$.)\n\n**Answer: (E) 1261**"
      }
