        "title": "Group in fours",
        "body": "Any four consecutive powers of 2 sum to $2^k(1+2+4+8)=15\\cdot2^k$, a multiple of 5. There are 2000 terms $=500$ groups of four, so the sum is a multiple of 5 and the remainder is 0. (Also, the sum equals $2^{2000}-1=16^{500}-1\\equiv1-1=0\\pmod5$.)\n\n**Answer: (A) 0**"
