    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Bound the remainder",
        "body": "With digit sum $s$ the remainder is at most $s-1$, and a two-digit number has $s\\le18$. For $s=18$ ($99$) the remainder is $9$. For $s=17$ (numbers 89, 98): $89=5\\cdot17+4$, $98=5\\cdot17+13$, remainders 4 and 13. For $s=16$ (79, 88, 97): $79=4\\cdot16+15$ gives remainder 15; the others give 8 and 1. Smaller $s$ give remainders at most $s-1\\le14$. So the maximum is 15.\n\n**Answer: (C) 15**"
      }
